## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical integration of image provenance with runtime attestation, ensuring defense in depth for CNF deployments in multi-region clusters.

## Key Concepts
- Image signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- SPDX SBOM association and SBOM validation
- In-cluster attestation service generating verifiable tokens
- Admission control enforcing both provenance and attestation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: basic attestation gate
function attest(imageDigest, token, sbom) {
  if (!verifySignature(imageDigest)) return false;
  if (!verifySBOM(sbom)) return false;
  if (!verifyToken(token)) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle key rotation and revocation in the KMS?
- How would you simulate attestation failures in a namespace to verify policy behavior?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design runtime policy reconfiguration with multi-tenant separation and zero-downtime updates.

## Key Concepts
- Central policy streaming via gRPC
- Per-tenant policy data model with versioning
- In-memory delta application with TTL and idempotence
- CRD design for policy declarations and rollout path

## Code Example
```proto
syntax = "proto3";
package policy;
message PolicyDelta {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string path_hash = 2;
  uint32 rate_limit = 3;
  uint32 window_seconds = 4;
  uint32 circuit_failure_limit = 5;
  uint32 circuit_reset_seconds = 6;
  uint32 log_sample_rate = 7;
  string policy_version = 8;
}
service PolicyService {
  rpc StreamPolicy(PolicyDelta) returns (stream PolicyDelta);
}
```

